asr-000015
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:29.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you. Today the Committee on Finance, Subcommittee H, will deliberate the budget proposal of the Department of Foreign Affairs and its attached agencies, namely the Foreign Service Institute,

asr-000016
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:59.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: the Presidential Commission on Visiting Forces, and the UNESCO National Commission of the Philippines. Under Republic Act No. 12314, the DFA was given a 28.32 billion budget for fiscal year 2026. For fiscal year 2027, the department is requesting 34.88 billion,

asr-000017
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:29.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: broken down into 34.62 billion for the Office of the Secretary, 161.7 million for the Foreign Service Institute, 51.4 million for the Presidential Commission on Visiting Forces, and 50.9 million for the UNESCO National Commission. The DFA is more than a government agency that issues passports, processes visas and conducts diplomacy. For more than 10 million Filipinos abroad, the DFA is the

asr-000018
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:59.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Philippine government when they are farthest from home. Kapag may gyera, sakuna, pagkakakulong, pang-aabuso, anumang krisis, ang Pilipino ay umaasa po sa ating gobyerno. At sa mga oras na pinakamahirap at pinakamapanganib, the DFA must be more than a presence abroad. It must be a government that responds, protects, and brings its people home. Therefore, our test today is to ensure that the proposed 34.88 billion budget

asr-000019
00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:19.320
